  {
   "slug": "about",
   "title": "Our story",
   "content": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:about}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:about}}\" alt=\"The studio table with fabric swatches\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:about}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Threadline started at a kitchen table with a roll of linen and a simple idea: make fewer, better clothes, and make them in the open. We work with a handful of family-run mills and workshops we know by name, and we price our pieces fairly, without seasonal mark-ups and mark-downs.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What we promise</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul><li>Natural and recycled fibres only.</li><li>Free repairs for the first year.</li><li>Free returns within 30 days.</li></ul><!-- /wp:list -->"
  },
  {
   "slug": "contact",
   "title": "Contact",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Questions about sizing, an order or a repair? Write to us and a real person answers within one working day.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>Email:</strong> hello@threadline.example<br><strong>Studio:</strong> 14 Weaver Lane, open Thursday to Saturday, 10–18.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
